We should use a Deployment, not a raw Pod.
This is how config-driven outages happen in real systems

What happens:

Pod is deleted
Deployment recreates it automatically
New pod reads bad config


👉 App is now misconfigured
👉 Kubernetes shows Running
👉 Infra is healthy, app logic is broken

This is a very common production outage.

# Observe the Failure Pattern (Senior Thinking)

Ask yourself:

Are nodes healthy? ✅
Are pods running? ✅
Are services broken? ❌
Is config valid? ❌

👉 This is why config outages are hard to detect.
